# 0018-qsa-index-reuse.patch — QSA sparse-index selection reuse across later decode rows of a request.
#
# What/why
#   QSA decode is compute-bound at the measured ~519k context: _scores scores every
#   row against every completed history block (~128k blocks at 512k with ratio 4).
#   Under the MTP chain only the verify row runs QSA per step (draft rows use the
#   draft head), so each step re-runs the full-history indexer for one row.
#   This patch carries the selected block indices per pooled-cache tensor (therefore
#   per stream, attention layer, and main/MTP cache) forward to later rows of the
#   same decode.  A row with no newly completed block copies the prior selection
#   without launching an indexer kernel; a row that completed new blocks scores
#   only the prior TOP candidates plus the new blocks, then reselects TOP.
#   It does not reuse raw scores.
#
# Expected effect
#   With index_budget=2048 and index_compress_ratio=4 (TOP=512 blocks), every
#   verify row after the first reuses the ring: the ring's validity requires only
#   that the row's end moved strictly forward and no block was un-completed
#   (a rejection or resize that moves end backwards, a dense row, or a replaced
#   pooled cache falls back to the original full score+select and recaptures the
#   ring).  The full-history _scores launch is removed for almost every decode
#   row, so decode tok/s should rise while the attention value/chunk kernels
#   remain unchanged.  Prefill explicitly bypasses it (reuse=False).
#
# Approximation (intentional, bounded)
#   The inherited TOP block IDs form the candidate set; blocks omitted by the
#   previous row cannot enter this row (they can re-enter at a later boundary
#   row that is fully rescored after a fallback).  With MTP steps of a handful
#   of tokens the candidate set is stale by at most a few new blocks per step;
#   the selected set remains TOP of the candidates, the same published
#   approximation as sglang's should_reuse_mtp_sparse_indices.
#   The needle/vision harness remains the correctness gate; mtp_yield must not drop.
#
# A/B
#   TENSORFOLD_QSA_REUSE=1 (default) enables this path; =0 returns to the existing
#   per-row full scoring path byte-for-byte in its original branch.
#
# Verification
#   Run fixup_patch.py, then verify_build_patch.py; the latter reapplies all baked
#   patches and import-gates the patched family inside the live image.

